{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1504613-black-spiral-dancers-polemic","id":1504613,"title":"Black Spiral Dancers Polemic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-06T10:43:04-08:00","id":1504613,"title":"Black Spiral Dancers Polemic","content":"I know this may sound silly, but there was this situation with an acquaintance of mine who was the storyteller of a chronicle involving the BSD, but he accepted a new guy and I don't know how that proceeded, but it seems that he brought up that the name Black Spiral Dancers, is problematic, so they just called it Spiral Dancers for a while. So, I personally don't think there's a problem with the BSD name, but I wanted to know if anyone knows if this is really a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T10:56:31-08:00","id":1504614,"title":"","content":"Just call them Dancers of the Dark Spiral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T11:36:24-08:00","id":1504616,"title":"","content":"I'm not really sure how &quot;Black Spiral Dancers&quot; as a name is problematic? Can I get more information about the reasons this guy has for the name being problematic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T13:17:59-08:00","id":1504628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1504613-black-spiral-dancers-polemic?p=1504616#post1504616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure how &quot;Black Spiral Dancers&quot; as a name is problematic? Can I get more information about the reasons this guy has for the name being problematic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Black Spiral Dancers are the bad guys and have &quot;Black&quot; in their name, and for some people, unleast was what a heard, is this would be a way to make people of African descent and darker skinned people in general look like villains just because of their skin color. I thought it was forced, but nowadays I've seen people get offended by less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T13:23:48-08:00","id":1504630,"title":"","content":"Sounds made up, its like a Caucasian complaining about white walkers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T13:46:21-08:00","id":1504634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1504613-black-spiral-dancers-polemic?p=1504630#post1504630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds made up, its like a Caucasian complaining about white walkers</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it sounds ridiculous, but like I said, I've seen worse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T13:46:52-08:00","id":1504635,"title":"","content":"I'll take a stab a guess:<br /> <br /> There's a long standing and on-going with more prominence now discussion in fantasy, and speculative fiction (which covers most RPGs) about how tainted the &quot;white = good, black = bad,&quot; tropes have become. Despite the fact that these are very old metaphors that long predate most modern cultures and easily stem back to some innate instinctual matters (perhaps a more universal way of saying it would be &quot;bright = good, shadowy = bad,&quot; because we're rather visually oriented in our assessment of the world around us), European and European derived cultures have struggled with not conflating these things with religion, ethnic stereotypes, and racism.<br /> <br /> Lord of the Rings, and a lot of fantasy media that's copied it uncritically, demonstrates how easy it is to fall into this sort of world building even of not intentionally. The basic idea of Eru and his Valar being associated with light facing off against Melkor and his forces of darkness isn't really a problem as a fictional mythology goes. But when you start to look into how the details ended up getting constructed (whether planned for or added later to explain things) there are some pretty odd things that come about. The elves, who actually meet the equivalent of angels and fought the equivalent of demons only really worked to spread the factual metaphysics of their world to Middle Earth (where the Elves first came into existence even if most when to Valinor later), and largely left humans in other places ignorant. The Maiar (aka the angels that would become the wizards) ended up putting some efforts into going farther afield (the Blues) but generally prioritized Middle Earth as well. Middle Earth is also basically Arda's version of Europe, where the other areas where humans lived in the world are, if very briefly, described as mixes of Africa and the Middle East. So all of the dark skinned humans in the world weren't followers of Eru (who's directly based on Abhrahamic monotheism with very strong Christian focus), and were thus more easily corrupted by Sauron. Which is.. kinda problematic: if you're not ethnically European and Christian... you're more morally compromised. It's not a great look; esp with some of the dominant strains of racism at the time these things were being written.<br /> <br /> As such, there are people that do tend to feel that using the &quot;white = good, black = bad,&quot; stuff is problematically tainted by a pretty long history of conflating it with more direct social ills than just being a basic mythological narrative. IME most people that delve into this recognize there's a spectrum and &quot;evil thing is black&quot; isn't inherently problematic; but it is worthy of at least a critical analysis to see if its falling for some of the pitfalls we see in fantasy fiction.<br /> <br /> I personally don't think the BSDs fail such a test on closer inspection. Nothing about them stretches into the idea that specific groups - esp. minorities - are inferior in some way. Dark skinned people aren't more prone to dancing the spiral just because both can be labelled black.<br /> <br /> There's a ton of problematic content in the WoD, and WtA is far to often a poster child for that instead of the exception, but this specific critique doesn't seem like it holds up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T08:46:55-08:00","id":1504847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1504613-black-spiral-dancers-polemic?p=1504635#post1504635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll take a stab a guess:<br /> <br /> There's a long standing and on-going with more prominence now discussion in fantasy, and speculative fiction (which covers most RPGs) about how tainted the &quot;white = good, black = bad,&quot; tropes have become. Despite the fact that these are very old metaphors that long predate most modern cultures and easily stem back to some innate instinctual matters (perhaps a more universal way of saying it would be &quot;bright = good, shadowy = bad,&quot; because we're rather visually oriented in our assessment of the world around us), European and European derived cultures have struggled with not conflating these things with religion, ethnic stereotypes, and racism.<br /> <br /> Lord of the Rings, and a lot of fantasy media that's copied it uncritically, demonstrates how easy it is to fall into this sort of world building even of not intentionally. The basic idea of Eru and his Valar being associated with light facing off against Melkor and his forces of darkness isn't really a problem as a fictional mythology goes. But when you start to look into how the details ended up getting constructed (whether planned for or added later to explain things) there are some pretty odd things that come about. The elves, who actually meet the equivalent of angels and fought the equivalent of demons only really worked to spread the factual metaphysics of their world to Middle Earth (where the Elves first came into existence even if most when to Valinor later), and largely left humans in other places ignorant. The Maiar (aka the angels that would become the wizards) ended up putting some efforts into going farther afield (the Blues) but generally prioritized Middle Earth as well. Middle Earth is also basically Arda's version of Europe, where the other areas where humans lived in the world are, if very briefly, described as mixes of Africa and the Middle East. So all of the dark skinned humans in the world weren't followers of Eru (who's directly based on Abhrahamic monotheism with very strong Christian focus), and were thus more easily corrupted by Sauron. Which is.. kinda problematic: if you're not ethnically European and Christian... you're more morally compromised. It's not a great look; esp with some of the dominant strains of racism at the time these things were being written.<br /> <br /> As such, there are people that do tend to feel that using the &quot;white = good, black = bad,&quot; stuff is problematically tainted by a pretty long history of conflating it with more direct social ills than just being a basic mythological narrative. IME most people that delve into this recognize there's a spectrum and &quot;evil thing is black&quot; isn't inherently problematic; but it is worthy of at least a critical analysis to see if its falling for some of the pitfalls we see in fantasy fiction.<br /> <br /> I personally don't think the BSDs fail such a test on closer inspection. Nothing about them stretches into the idea that specific groups - esp. minorities - are inferior in some way. Dark skinned people aren't more prone to dancing the spiral just because both can be labelled black.<br /> <br /> There's a ton of problematic content in the WoD, and WtA is far too often a poster child for that instead of the exception, but this specific critique doesn't seem like it holds up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> in their analysis and conclusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}